WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.229
One of the biggest, uh, geopolitical blunders
of this administration has been Donald Trump

00:00:06.229 --> 00:00:11.570
sailing on the Iran nuclear deal. Importantly,
without Iran having violated the deal, which

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:16.059
was of course signed under President Barack
Obama. And you might remember as many people

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:21.330
did Trump opposed the deal under Obama. Lots
of right wingers did that and that's fine.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:27.060
But once the deal signed Willy Nilly canceling
it when you're elected president, absent any

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.640
caused to do so based on what's in the deal
is not a good idea. And I've said this before,

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.410
if other countries can't trust that the United
States is going to stick to the deals that

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:41.940
we make, even when a president changes, when
the party in the, uh, controlling the White

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:48.200
House changes, there is no incentive to deal
with us. There is no incentive to treat us

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.370
correctly. It's geo politically a disaster.
And that's exactly what it has been. I also

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.629
told you several weeks ago that Iran completely
predictably is now resuming nuclear research

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:04.559
and development possibly for nuclear energy,
possibly for nuclear weapons, which of course

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:05.920
I don't want them to have.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:11.850
But the point is they're resuming enrichment
of uranium, which I don't want them to do.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.450
But given the circumstances, it's perfectly
logical. It's perfectly rational. And it's

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:23.330
what we would expect that they would do. Iran
knows that if they are not, uh, if the United

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:29.020
States has bailed on the Iran nuclear deal,
they are better off no matter what happens

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.649
in the future. Starting to enrich uranium
again, either they start arranging uranium

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:40.290
so that in the future it becomes a negotiating
point for a future deal. Or they start enriching

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:45.409
uranium either to develop nuclear power or
nuclear weapons. Because if they understand

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:53.140
history, they know that historically having
nuclear weapons has been a strong positioning

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:58.689
item positioning. It has been strong for the
positioning of nations. And there are numerous

00:01:58.689 --> 00:02:02.910
examples that we can look at and those include,
uh, we've talked about Iraq, we've talked

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.799
about many others, so it's completely predictable
that it's what Iran would do.

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:09.950
I don't want them to do it, but I get why
they're doing it. And what Donald Trump is

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:14.140
now doing is trying to have it both ways.
Trump has bailed on the deal. He has pulled

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:19.380
the United States out of the Iran nuclear
deal, but at the same time is demanding that

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:24.709
Iran stick to the deal unless they want to
face further consequences for not sticking

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:28.319
to the deal. And here's the loophole that
the Trump administration is trying to use

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:33.940
to justify this nonsense. What the U S is
saying is that even though we pulled out of

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.680
the deal, there are other countries that are
still in the deal. And this is of course the

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:44.290
height of absurdity, the uh, the Donald Trump
back to the United States out of the Iran

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:49.920
nuclear deal. It was a coalition deal. So
the argument they're making is the u s is

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:55.390
out, but Iran is still in the deal with the
UK and with France and with Germany.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.220
And of course on a technical level that may
be, but then it's up to those countries to

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:05.739
demand that Iran comply. Donald Trump and
the United States have no credibility whatsoever

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:09.959
to even ask for that. At this point in time,
and even worse, is that the United States

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.700
has actually made it almost impossible for
the other countries to keep working with Iran

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:21.450
on compliance. So Donald Trump has sort of
put himself into a very strange and idiotic

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:27.989
coroner, but specifically a corner that lacks
all credibility on the issue. And unfortunately,

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:32.780
and this really is a problem, there are news
outlets that are reporting that Iran would

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:40.080
be in violation of the deal if they do this
or if they did that Trump ripped up the agreement.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:46.690
It makes it hard for other countries to keep
it going. Uh, uh, when Donald Trump does that,

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:50.920
and then yet he still insists that Iran has
to stick with the deal.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:56.170
And more importantly, maybe we're used to
Trump's hypocrisy and idiocy and ignorance

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:02.930
domestically, but geo politically, this starts
to put Europe once again, potentially at odds

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:08.190
with the United States because ultimately
those other countries, the European signatories

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:13.820
to the Iran deal might have to say, we agree
with the u s even though Trump backed out,

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:19.500
the deal with, uh, us is still on and Iran
needs to abide by it. That would be taking

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:25.620
Trump's side when it comes to this disagreement
or the European signatories might say, even

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:31.420
though this is a multipart deal, by ripping
it up as far as American involvement, the

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:37.460
deal is effectively dead. And we really have
no sort of compliance authority to enforce

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:43.350
that Iran stick to it. And this is yet another
one of these examples of how the United States

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:48.590
will be pitted against Europe. And we've talked
about this before, when the US and Europe

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:54.160
are at odds, this is a win for Putin who wants
to put a wedge between the United States and

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.160
our allies.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:05:03.010
A lot of petitions, prerogatives and priorities
when it comes to NATO, uh, relate to driving

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:08.370
a wedge between the United States and Europe.
This relates to so much of what we've been

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.970
talking about over the last couple of years,
and it's not this cartoonish Trump and Putin

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:17.500
colluding thing. It's that Donald Trump doesn't
even have the wherewithal and the knowledge

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:23.520
and the intelligence, quite frankly, to even
understand the ways in which his actions and

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:29.850
statements regarding Europe and other allies
and his looking away when it's convenient

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:36.900
to look away from authoritarian leaders doing
absolutely terrible things. It all fits into

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:44.310
a politic that benefits Vladimir Putin in
a world in which Russia and China are increasingly

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:50.470
aligned to the detriment of the United States
as sort of the third leg of the nucleus of

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:54.740
the super powers, the three growing geopolitical
superpowers. And we've talked about this many,

00:05:54.740 --> 00:06:00.920
many times before. It doesn't have to be Trump
colluding with Putin to be executing a politic

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:06.090
that benefits Putin in ways that Russia has
been thinking about and talking about at least

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.510
for two plus decades, if not longer.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:14.280
This in the end is going to be what it's about.
We'd be better off if Donald Trump had not

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.370
backed out of the deal. Iran would be further
back in their nuclear development. Everyone

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:27.110
would be safer, uh, with an Iran that is still
part of the deal and complying with the Iran

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:33.060
nuclear deal. Instead, we have an Iran that
is newly invigorated in its nuclear development.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:38.420
There are new discussions of war with Iran
on the table, and it's absolutely absurd and

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:42.890
utterly embarrassing on the national stage,
which has basically been the theme of this

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:48.500
administration. If you disagree, uh, let me
know. I want to hear from you about the Iran

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:54.020
nuclear deal, about Iran's actions in resuming
enrichment of uranium, uh, about the context

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:59.990
in which Putin likes the idea of the United
States at odds with Europe, about what does

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:04.213
or doesn't Iran have to do with regard to
what is remaining the Tatars of the Iran nuclear

00:07:04.213 --> 00:07:05.213
deal.

00:07:05.213 --> 00:07:05.219
Let me know what you think.

